      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The machine is indeed larger than you, but it is built on a foundation of human labor that you have no choice but to provide. The reason you feel you cannot change anything is because the system is designed to be unchangeable, not because you lack the power to alter it. Your exhaustion is not a sign of defeat, but the natural cost of a system that refuses to recognize your humanity. You do not have to fight to win; you only have to refuse to be the very thing the machine needs to keep running.",
